            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The eschatological end of the age and final judgment, encompassing both the ingathering of the righteous and the sorting out of the wicked.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Matthew 13:30\",\"Matthew 13:39\",\"Revelation 14:14-16\",\"Joel 3:13\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Evangelism, missionary work, and the immediate ingathering of souls for salvation.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 9:37-38\",\"Luke 10:2\",\"John 4:35\"],\"prominence\":\"dominant\"},{\"meaning\":\"Spiritual, moral, or material rewards based on one's actions (the principle of sowing and reaping).\",\"basis\":[\"Galatians 6:7-9\",\"2 Corinthians 9:6-10\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Strictly the outpouring of God's wrath and punishment upon the wicked (often depicted as a grape harvest or vintage).\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 14:18-20\",\"Isaiah 63:1-6\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The symbol of the harvest is highly stable in Christian interpretation, carrying a dual primary application: the eschatological final judgment and the ongoing mission of the Church to evangelize. Both are explicitly defined by Jesus in the Gospels and are widely accepted across interpretive traditions.\"}",
